the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing Two Syllables Back From the Suffix: -ate"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you learn new words, it is important that you know which part of the word to stress. In words with the suffix <span class=\"italic\"> -ate</span>, the stress falls two syllables back from the <span class=\"italic\"> -ate</span> ending."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Suffixes, or word endings, can help you to decide where to place the stress in the word. Placing stress on the correct syllables will help others to better understand you when speaking."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For words with the suffix <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">-ate</span></span>, you should count two syllables back from the ending of the word and place the stress on that syllable."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"operate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">o</span> - per - ate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"populate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">po</span> - pu - late\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"contaminate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"con -  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ta</span>  - mi  - nate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discriminate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"dis  - <span class=\\\"strong\\\">cri</span>  - mi  -  nate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"navigate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">nav</span> - i - gate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"approximate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" ap-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">prox</span>-i-mate\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use this rule for any word ending in <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">\u2013ate</span></span>, even if the word is a long word."}, {"type": "example", "content": "appreciate"}, {"type": "example", "content": "locate  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "dominates "}, {"type": "example", "content": "associate"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Using Homographs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Homographs are words that sometimes sound the same and are spelled the same."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a two syllable homograph like <span class=\"italic\"> permit</span> the stress falls on the first syllable if it is a noun and it falls on the second syllable if it is a verb."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Noun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"point\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a specific place\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to indicate with one's finger\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"permit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a document that allows permission\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to allow someone to do something\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"minute\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a portion of time\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"very small\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the part that remains\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to relax\\\"}\",\"\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to permit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to allow"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Also the authorities do not permit eating or drinking while on the premises. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about stargazing."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "minute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very small"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Binoculars that can help you see what is minute to the naked eye."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to congregate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to gather together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A visible pattern of stars congregates to form a constellation.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to associate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to have contact with or connection to"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Travellers and sailors often associate this star with the North Pole."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to isolate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to separate from"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's much easier to locate stars when you don't isolate or separate them. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le01ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le01ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Go online or to your local library and find a list of 10 homographs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Check their definitions in a dictionary and find out whether they are verbs, adjectives, nouns, adverbs, etc. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Check their pronunciation in the dictionary or with your instructor."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a poem about the stars or a topic you like. Use at least 3 pairs of homographs in the poem."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading the poem aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research words that are spelled the same but have different meaning and/or pronunciation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a poem using words that are spelled the same but have different meaning and/or pronunciation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the poem aloud."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le01ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le01ob04re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">A Guided Tour of the Stars</span><br>\n<br>\nHello everybody!  Welcome to the annual stargazing tour! Before we start our tour I must tell you that I will stamp your parking permits at the end of the tour. Also the authorities do not permit eating or drinking while on the premises.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le01ob04re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "I really appreciate that everyone made it out today. I'll be your guide for this evening. We're going to locate as many stars and constellations as we can. In a minute, I will hand out sets of binoculars that can help you see what is minute to the naked eye. We are going to start with the first star whose brightness dominates the rest.  When you rest your eyes on this star, you'll know that you have found the North Star also known as \u201cPolaris\u201d.", "id": 2, "time": "20000", "image": "engenn10le01ob04re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "They say it is the closest star to the celestial poles, which lie to the North and South. Travelers and sailors often associate this star with the North Pole, serving as a strong reference point as they navigate from one place to another.  If you ever become lost at sea, this star can definitely point you in the right direction. You may also see that Polaris is part of a visible pattern of stars that congregate to form a constellation. The constellation you see here is called \u201cUrsa Minor\u201d, which is also known as the \u201cLittle Dipper\u201d.", "id": 3, "time": "47000", "image": "engenn10le01ob04re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "If you see a constellation of stars resembling a small ladle, you will know you have found the \u201cLittle Dipper\u201d ... If you have problems finding Polaris, look for this constellation and you will find Polaris right on its handle. It's much easier to locate stars when you don't isolate or separate them. <br/><br/>Let's move on to the next star ...", "id": 4, "time": "82500", "image": "engenn10le01ob04re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about science and leisure time. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can say and use words like <span class=\"italic\">appreciate</span> and <span class=\"italic\">associate</span>."}, {"type": "Learning 